---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Story — Virtue Literacy Africa"
  description="How Virtue Literacy Africa emerged from Virtue Books, what drives us, and the problem we exist to solve in Africa's informal settlements."
  currentPage="/about"
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Our Story</span>
      <h1>Founded on a conviction: storytelling can transform communities.</h1>
      <p>Virtue Literacy Africa began with a book and a settlement. It grew into a five-pillar programme built on documentation, mobile access, civic education, and the belief that every child deserves the tools to lead.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BACKGROUND & INSPIRATION -->
  <section class="background-section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <span class="kicker">Background &amp; Inspiration</span>
      <h2>Where we came from.</h2>
      <p>Virtue Literacy Africa is an initiative of <a href="https://virtuebooks.co.ke" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--ink);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:var(--accent)">Virtue Books</a>, a Nairobi-based publisher committed to producing values-based, civic, and accessible books for African children. In 2024, Virtue Books published <em>Place Called Kibera</em> — a documentary title capturing life in one of Nairobi's largest informal settlements through first-person accounts and photography.</p>
      <p>That experience revealed both the depth of the literacy gap in informal settlements and the potential of storytelling as a tool for civic awakening. It also demonstrated the power of documentation: seeing a community clearly, on its own terms, before attempting to serve it.</p>
      <p>VLA was founded to expand that social mandate — to move beyond publishing into active, on-the-ground delivery of literacy, civic education, and technology access in the communities that need them most.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        <span class="callout-label">About Place Called Kibera</span>
        <h3>The book that started it all</h3>
        <p><em>Place Called Kibera</em> (Virtue Books, 2024) is a first-person narrative and photo documentary of life in Nairobi's Kibera informal settlement. It remains the foundation of VLA's commitment to documentation as the first act of civic literacy — and the first of what will become a growing library of settlement documentation titles.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROBLEM STATEMENT -->
  <section class="problem">
    <div class="container grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="kicker">The Problem</span>
        <h2>Potential, capped before a child can read.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="plist reveal">
        <li><span class="x">/</span><span>Severely limited access to books, reading materials, and enriching content.</span></li>
        <li><span class="x">/</span><span>Few safe, stimulating spaces for learning and creative expression.</span></li>
        <li><span class="x">/</span><span>Little exposure to values-based education that builds character and resilience.</span></li>
        <li><span class="x">/</span><span>Near-total absence of civic education — no sense of rights, or the power to use them.</span></li>
        <li><span class="x">/</span><span>Growing disconnect between children and the communities that will one day rely on them to lead.</span></li>
        <li><span class="x">/</span><span>Rapid AI adoption threatens to deepen the digital and literacy divide unless inclusive tools are developed intentionally.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="container" style="margin-top:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.5rem)">
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);max-width:64ch;line-height:1.75">Without deliberate intervention, the cycle repeats: limited literacy leads to limited civic awareness, which leads to limited agency. Virtue Literacy Africa exists to interrupt that cycle — through books, mobile libraries, civic events, AI tools, and the young leaders who will become the most powerful agents of community transformation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- VISION & MISSION -->
  <section class="vm-section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Our Foundation</span>
      <div class="vm-grid">
        <div class="vm-cell">
          <span class="vm-label">Vision</span>
          <h3>An Africa where every child, regardless of where they were born, has access to books, knowledge, and the tools to shape their future.</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="vm-cell">
          <span class="vm-label">Mission</span>
          <p>To document Africa's informal settlement realities and respond with mobile libraries, literacy events, civic education, values-based books, and AI learning fellowships — nurturing children who are not only literate, but informed, empowered, and ready to lead.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TARGET BENEFICIARIES -->
  <section class="beneficiaries-section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Who We Serve</span>
      <h2>Target beneficiaries.</h2>
      <ul class="beneficiaries">
        <li>
          <span class="bn">01</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Children aged 5&ndash;17</h4>
            <p>Children in Nairobi's informal settlements — Phase 1 focuses on Kibera, Mathare, and Korogocho.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">02</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Young people aged 18&ndash;28</h4>
            <p>Particularly aspiring civic leaders and AI enthusiasts, targeted through the AI Learning Fellowships programme.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">03</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Caregivers, parents, and community teachers</h4>
            <p>Adults who support children's learning at home and in informal school settings, including as primary users of the Mwangaza AI tool.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">04</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Persons with disabilities</h4>
            <p>Including children and caregivers navigating accessibility barriers in education and reading materials.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.2rem">Phase 1 focuses on Nairobi. Phase 2 and beyond aim to scale to other Kenyan counties and eventually across Africa.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- IMPLEMENTATION PHASES -->
  <section class="phases-section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Implementation Approach</span>
      <h2>A phased, scalable model.</h2>
      <table class="phases-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Phase</th>
            <th>Timeline</th>
            <th>Geography</th>
            <th>Key Deliverables</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Phase"><span class="phase-name">Phase 1<span>Foundation</span></span></td>
            <td data-label="Timeline">Year 1&ndash;2</td>
            <td data-label="Geography">3 Nairobi settlements: Kibera, Mathare, Korogocho</td>
            <td data-label="Key Deliverables">2 mobile library units; 2 new VLA books published; 3 civic education events; 1 AI fellowship cohort; Mwangaza AI pilot</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Phase"><span class="phase-name">Phase 2<span>Scale</span></span></td>
            <td data-label="Timeline">Year 3&ndash;5</td>
            <td data-label="Geography">Additional Kenyan counties</td>
            <td data-label="Key Deliverables">Expanded mobile library fleet; fellowship programme growth; 4 additional VLA titles; Mwangaza AI v2 with multilingual support</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Phase"><span class="phase-name">Phase 3<span>Pan-African</span></span></td>
            <td data-label="Timeline">Year 5+</td>
            <td data-label="Geography">Pan-African</td>
            <td data-label="Key Deliverables">Continental AI curriculum partnership; multilingual book series; diaspora fellowship track</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="act">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Be part of it.</h2>
      <div class="act-grid reveal">
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Partner with us</h3>
          <p>Financial sponsors, in-kind donors, institutional partners, and governance organisations.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/get-involved">See how to get involved &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Volunteer</h3>
          <p>Illustrators, educators, AI practitioners, health workers, and storytellers.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/get-involved">Give your skills &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Contact us</h3>
          <p>Questions, media enquiries, or just a conversation about what we are building.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/contact">Get in touch &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
